{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792249191,"nonce":"MIm5dmY60Y975D7nt8g8jj4HYd4=","message":"Fixed in 7944fa75b76dfeab0afab288695f6dcd24c5e480. ash_wasm_link::dylink::expose_memory re-exports a side module's imported memory as 'memory' before the native loader compiles it, so the host's WASI functions find it on the calling instance. Checked with ashui's blinc_abi.wasm and smoke.wasm: on the shared binary it traps in random_get with 'missing required memory export'; on a host built from this change it runs its checks to the end. Unit tests in ash_wasm_link/tests/side_module_memory.rs cover the failure, the fix, and the two no-op cases (memory already exported; no imported memory). Not covered: the browser host, which does not reach WASI through the calling instance.","files":null}]}